9. Attention Mechanism

Attention is one of the most important concepts in Transformers.

Attention allows the model to determine which parts of the input are important when processing a particular token.

Example

Consider:

The animal didn't cross the road because it was tired.

The model needs to understand relationships between different words.

Attention helps the model consider relevant context.

Simplified View
Token 1 ───────┐
Token 2 ───────┤
Token 3 ───────┼──→ Attention
Token 4 ───────┤
Token 5 ───────┘
                  ↓
          Context Information
Self-Attention

In self-attention, tokens in the same sequence can attend to other tokens.

The mechanism commonly uses:

Q = Query
K = Key
V = Value

The mathematical formula is:

Attention(Q, K, V)
=
softmax(QKᵀ / √dₖ)V

For beginners, don't focus on memorizing the formula.

Understand this:

Attention helps the model determine how much importance one token should give to other tokens.

