19. Tokens

LLMs generally process tokens, not raw text directly.

A token can be:

A complete word
Part of a word
Punctuation
A symbol
A subword

Example:

"unbelievable"

could conceptually be split into:

un + believ + able

The exact tokenization depends on the tokenizer.

